  "description": "<p>Currently, GET-ting a binary resource always includes the <em>content-disposition: attachment</em> header (plus other related information), triggering a download prompt in the browser and making it impossible to examine suitable resources directly inline. </p>\n\n<p>There is also an old Fedora 4.X issue concerning this: <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-1843\" title=\"smart-link\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-1843</a> </p>",
